(1525698, 198803, 20330, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yurasocolov:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh boy... <br/>Edit: let me elaborate. I think swiping ideas from previous challenge winners is just lame, even if you enhance it a little by adding a bug or two. So, sorry, no ''unbelievable'', ''creative'' and ''wonderful'' from me: <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=102761" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/253/thumb/102761.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/253/thumb/102761.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/253/thumb/102761.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I do not agree. Hats off to ya! This is a learning community, if we did not try to repeat some aspects of others works then how are we ever to learn? And, it is SO not nice to call someone lame. Some people here need to grow up and stop taking away from the winners the joy they so richly deserve! :) Looks to me like yurasocolov likes to reflect things in droplets of water also: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=129478" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/288/thumb/129478.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/288/thumb/129478.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/288/thumb/129478.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-11 06:16:19.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by yurasocolov: Oh boy... Edit: let me elaborate. I think swiping ideas from previous challenge winners is just lame, even if you enhance it a little by adding a bug or two. So, sorry, no ''unbelievable'', ''creative'' and ''wonderful'' from me:    I do not agree. Hats off to ya! This is a learning community, if we did not try to repeat some aspects of others works then how are we ever to learn? And, it is SO not nice to call someone lame. Some people here need to grow up and stop taking away from the winners the joy they so richly deserve! :) Looks to me like yurasocolov likes to reflect things in droplets of water also: ', '2005-07-11 07:12:40.000000', '2005-07-11 07:16:19.000000', 0),
(1525700, 199345, 19746, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get around to commenting but I''m a little disappointed that this ended up all the way down here.  Terrific feel to this shot and it was great to see something original against all the bugs and flowers out there.<br/> <br/>I gave you an 8, at least you scored 6+ :)<br/> <br/>Alex</td>', 'I didn''t get around to commenting but I''m a little disappointed that this ended up all the way down here.  Terrific feel to this shot and it was great to see something original against all the bugs and flowers out there. I gave you an 8, at least you scored 6+ :) Alex', '2005-07-11 07:19:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1525811, 198557, 3569, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the kind comments.  The shot was one of seven outtakes and the only one where the dragonfly was facing semi-forward.  All I did was auto-focus on a hovering d-fly, and shoot.  In PS I added contrast, curved a bit and USMed.  I Neat Imaged the shot.  Van</td>', 'Thanks for the kind comments.  The shot was one of seven outtakes and the only one where the dragonfly was facing semi-forward.  All I did was auto-focus on a hovering d-fly, and shoot.  In PS I added contrast, curved a bit and USMed.  I Neat Imaged the shot.  Van', '2005-07-11 08:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
