(1527368, 198815, 2170, '<td valign="top">B/W Club!<br/> <br/>i think this is a nice still life.  i''m not sure that it makes the best duotone shot for a couple of reasons.  <br/> <br/>1) still lifes are normally color.  i''m all about breaking rules, but one kind of "expects" to see them that way.<br/> <br/>2) there are a couple of things in the photo that also are "expected" to be in color: the wine, flowers, and the oranges particularly.  again, anything CAN be in black and white -- the challenge is deciding what SHOULD be.<br/> <br/>i think the tones and contrast in this are pretty good.  yeah, there are blown-out bits, but i have no problem with those.</td>', 'B/W Club! i think this is a nice still life.  i''m not sure that it makes the best duotone shot for a couple of reasons.   1) still lifes are normally color.  i''m all about breaking rules, but one kind of "expects" to see them that way. 2) there are a couple of things in the photo that also are "expected" to be in color: the wine, flowers, and the oranges particularly.  again, anything CAN be in black and white -- the challenge is deciding what SHOULD be. i think the tones and contrast in this are pretty good.  yeah, there are blown-out bits, but i have no problem with those.', '2005-07-11 16:04:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1527382, 199447, 31738, '<td valign="top">This definitely deserved a BLUE!</td>', 'This definitely deserved a BLUE!', '2005-07-11 16:09:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1527404, 199291, 31738, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites. Great composition. They actually look like jumbo berries. I''m surprised this didn''t get a ribbon. Too bad =(<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-11 15:14:17.</i></td>', 'One of my favorites. Great composition. They actually look like jumbo berries. I''m surprised this didn''t get a ribbon. Too bad =(', '2005-07-11 16:13:26.000000', '2005-07-11 16:14:17.000000', 0),
(1527442, 198815, 14614, '<td valign="top">B/W Club! <br/> <br/>The rosy dual tone highlights the element that "normally" is that color (e.g. the wine in this case) and give the shot a bit of a romantic feel.  I''m wondering if rose/red/pink does that in general to shots.  I like the light and dark tonal variety in the main elements.  I''m wondering if you played around with the contrast (you notes don''t mention that you did) and what effect did it have?</td>', 'B/W Club!  The rosy dual tone highlights the element that "normally" is that color (e.g. the wine in this case) and give the shot a bit of a romantic feel.  I''m wondering if rose/red/pink does that in general to shots.  I like the light and dark tonal variety in the main elements.  I''m wondering if you played around with the contrast (you notes don''t mention that you did) and what effect did it have?', '2005-07-11 16:25:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1527591, 199315, 24137, '<td valign="top">This was one of my highest scoring shots. I thought it would place much higher. Imagineer said it perfectly --- Crazy.</td>', 'This was one of my highest scoring shots. I thought it would place much higher. Imagineer said it perfectly --- Crazy.', '2005-07-11 17:26:22.000000', NULL, 0),
