(1527880, 198803, 23458, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yurasocolov:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh boy... <br/>Edit: let me elaborate. I think swiping ideas from previous challenge winners is just lame, even if you enhance it a little by adding a bug or two. So, sorry, no ''unbelievable'', ''creative'' and ''wonderful'' from me: <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=102761" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/253/thumb/102761.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/253/thumb/102761.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/253/thumb/102761.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>See normally I''d agree with this sentiment - but after reading the photogs comment it''s pretty clear that this shot was taken with tongue firmly planted in cheek. Thus it''s really just a very well executed bit of dpc satire. <br/> <br/>It must have taken some doing to get both the waterdrop AND the bug to cooperate at the same time. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by yurasocolov: Oh boy... Edit: let me elaborate. I think swiping ideas from previous challenge winners is just lame, even if you enhance it a little by adding a bug or two. So, sorry, no ''unbelievable'', ''creative'' and ''wonderful'' from me:    See normally I''d agree with this sentiment - but after reading the photogs comment it''s pretty clear that this shot was taken with tongue firmly planted in cheek. Thus it''s really just a very well executed bit of dpc satire.  It must have taken some doing to get both the waterdrop AND the bug to cooperate at the same time.  ', '2005-07-11 19:17:23.000000', NULL, 0),
