(1536640, 198339, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Man did you pick a hard subject!! What I have noticed when I take a picture with very little light is that I get a lot of noise. I see that this is what happened to you too. The image is also out of focus. Not every picture has to be sharp and perfect, but for a macro challenge it should be. I am glad that you chose to go "out of the box". This is not a typical macro entry and that is refreshing. I think that you should practise more with low lighting. I really don''t know a lot about your camera to give you tips for that--I am sorry.</td>', '*Critique Club* Man did you pick a hard subject!! What I have noticed when I take a picture with very little light is that I get a lot of noise. I see that this is what happened to you too. The image is also out of focus. Not every picture has to be sharp and perfect, but for a macro challenge it should be. I am glad that you chose to go "out of the box". This is not a typical macro entry and that is refreshing. I think that you should practise more with low lighting. I really don''t know a lot about your camera to give you tips for that--I am sorry.', '2005-07-14 23:53:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1536671, 199594, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Well Joey, I am a big fan of yours!! This is very different! Like most all of your work, it is out of the box and unique. They still look like candy, but I really don''t think that matters. I think what hurt this photo was that it was out of focus. I know that was what you were going for but IMO a macro should be focused. That is what is so great about macros is the attention to details. I like the negative space and your arrangement of the candy, very nice. The colors are a little harsh, but that is a reflection of your style that I am familiar with. I get that you wanted the "soft" look because of the title, but I think that the theme would have been better for a different challenge. Great ideas like always, you are so creative. I hope that this was helpful.<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Well Joey, I am a big fan of yours!! This is very different! Like most all of your work, it is out of the box and unique. They still look like candy, but I really don''t think that matters. I think what hurt this photo was that it was out of focus. I know that was what you were going for but IMO a macro should be focused. That is what is so great about macros is the attention to details. I like the negative space and your arrangement of the candy, very nice. The colors are a little harsh, but that is a reflection of your style that I am familiar with. I get that you wanted the "soft" look because of the title, but I think that the theme would have been better for a different challenge. Great ideas like always, you are so creative. I hope that this was helpful. Mandy', '2005-07-15 00:07:53.000000', NULL, 0),
